flow "High-availability failover and split brain"
summary "Promotes a standby replica when the primary fails, using fencing (STONITH) to prevent two primaries from corrupting data during a partition."
tags high-availability failover fencing
level advanced
source "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Split-brain_(computing)"
related distributed-systems/leader-lease distributed-systems/distributed-lock-redlock

node client "Clients" actor
node p1 "Primary A" db tone=primary
node p2 "Standby B" db
node fence "Fencing Controller" service
node disk "Shared Storage" db
edge client > p1
edge client > p2 hidden
edge p1 > p2 noarrow
edge p1 > disk
edge p2 > disk
edge fence > p1 dashed
edge fence > p2 dashed
array roles "Cluster roles" keys=p1,p2 = Primary Standby

scenario clean-failover "Fenced failover preserves single writer"
  step replicate "Primary A serves writes and replicates to B"
    "In active-passive HA, only Primary A writes to storage and streams replication + heartbeats to Standby B."
    send client > p1 "WRITE x=1"
    send p1 > disk "x=1"
    send p1 > p2 "replicate + hb" with
    state p1,p2,disk success
  step fail-and-fence "Primary A fails; controller fences A first"
    "Primary A stops responding. Before promoting Standby B, the Fencing Controller cuts A's power or revokes its storage lease (**STONITH**: Shoot The Other Node In The Head)."
    detail "Hardware fencing eliminates ambiguity: power fencing shuts off the node through IPMI, a remote PDU, or a watchdog timer, while storage-level SCSI-3 persistent reservations revoke the node's reservation key so the SAN rejects any further I/O from it."
    state p1 error
    send fence > p1 "FENCE / power-off"
    label roles#p1 "FENCED"
    state roles#p1 error with
    callout fence "Confirm A is dead before promoting B"
  step promote "Standby B promotes safely to Primary"
    "Only after fencing confirms Primary A cannot touch storage does Standby B promote and take client traffic — guaranteeing a single writer."
    show client-p2
    label p2 "Primary B"
    label roles#p2 "Primary" with
    state p2 success
    send client > p2 "WRITE x=2"
    send p2 > disk "x=2"

scenario split-brain "Partition without fencing causes split brain" from=clean-failover/replicate
  step partition "Heartbeat link breaks while both nodes live"
    "The network link between A and B fails, so B stops hearing heartbeats — yet **Primary A is still alive** and accepting writes from clients!"
    detail "A strict majority quorum requires `floor(N/2) + 1` votes. In a two-node cluster, a link break splits the cluster 1 versus 1, so neither side holds a majority without an external witness or quorum device acting as a third tie-breaker."
    state p1-p2 error
    callout p2 "No heartbeat: thinks A is dead!"
  step dual-primary "Unfenced B promotes -> two active primaries"
    "Without fencing or a quorum tie-breaker, Standby B promotes itself to Primary. Now both A (`x=2`) and B (`x=9`) write conflicting updates to storage (**split brain**)."
    show client-p2
    label p2 "Primary B (rogue!)"
    label roles#p2 "Primary!" with
    state p1,p2,disk error
    effect disk shake
    send client > p1 "WRITE x=2"
    send client > p2 "WRITE x=9" with
    send p1 > disk "x=2"
    send p2 > disk "x=9 (CORRUPT!)" with
    callout disk "Split brain: dual writes corrupt data"
